{{/*
  investigation-handoff — the label contract that lets every investigation
  flow and every implementation flow coexist on the same bead. The label
  `implementation-refined` means: "an Investigation Report (see
  beads-issues/shared/investigate-report) is on the bead — problem
  decomposition, implementation instructions and code-not-to-touch are
  defined, so an implementer needs no further design work".

  Producers: beads-issues/investigate ("Investigate more"), beads/investigate-all-more,
  and the inner investigation phases of the loop drivers
  (Bug fix — investigate phase, Feature — plan phase).
  Consumers: the implementation phases (Bug fix — fix phase,
  Feature — implement phase) and the drivers' phase selection.

  Parameters (dict):
    Role — "producer": explains when to add the label.
           "consumer": explains how to recognise and use it.

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/investigation-handoff" (dict "Role" "producer") }}
*/}}
{{- if eq .Role "consumer" }}
**Refined beads.** If the bead carries the **`implementation-refined`** label, a prior investigation
already produced an Investigation Report (a `bd comment` plus the enriched description / acceptance /
design fields). Treat it as the authoritative spec: do **not** re-investigate or re-plan. Implement
exactly the **Implementation instructions** for each work unit in the report's **Problem
decomposition** order, change only the files and symbols the report names, and **never touch anything
listed under "Code not to touch"**. If the live code contradicts the report, or following it would
require touching excluded code, stop and defer (Step 4) instead of improvising.
{{- else }}
**Mark the result.** Add the **`implementation-refined`** label only when the report is genuinely
implementation-ready: every section is settled, the decomposition and implementation instructions are
concrete, and "Code not to touch" is explicit. Never add it to a bead you deferred or left with open
questions. The label lets other flows (and a later implementation phase, possibly run by a different
agent) recognise that the problem is already refined and skip straight to implementing the defined
changes. Never remove it, and keep any phase labels you are responsible for alongside it.
{{- end }}
